  "final_message": "The app is complete. Here's a summary of what I built:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask + SQLite under `./data`, with:\n- Auth: register (201), login (200 `{token}`), Bearer-token sessions; protected routes return 401.\n- Subscriptions: create, paged list (`q`/`status`/`plan`/`page`/`page_size`), get one, PATCH partial update.\n- Invoices: list (newest first), issue an open invoice.\n- Collections: `failed`/`succeeded` \u2014 success marks open invoices paid and resets `failed_payment_count`; failure increments it and flips active \u2192 past_due.\n- Public stats: MRR (sum of `monthly_amount` over active + past_due) and per-status counts, no auth.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`) \u2014 React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind v4, with React Router:\n- Public summary (MRR + status counts), register/sign-in forms, header with username + sign-out.\n- Subscription table with status tabs, plan filter, customer search, paging; detail page with edit form, invoice history, issue-invoice form, and record failed/succeeded buttons.\n\n**Verified:** typecheck (`tsc --noEmit`) and `npm run build` pass; the API behavior (auth, filters, MRR, collections) and static/SPA serving were tested against the real Flask app and gunicorn.\n\nNote: I added `typescript`, `@types/react`, `@types/react-dom` to devDependencies and pinned `tailwindcss`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `react-router-dom` (all resolved via `package-lock.json`). One thing worth flagging \u2014 the pre-existing `backend/requirements.lock` only pins the `backend/requirements.txt` packages, and I did not change backend dependencies, so it remains consistent.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
